HELP - THE ONLINE HELP COMMAND

CALLER. Subject to the current caller access policy.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
HELP - THE ONLINE HELP COMMAND

CALLER. Subject to the current caller access policy.

Syntax:
    HELP [dir:][helpname]
    HELP //

Without a name, opens the online help root. Example: HELP HELP:USER

Select the displayed menu letter. ^ returns one level; period returns to
the root of the current help session. When opened directly, that file is
the root. Space/pages and the displayed prompts control long text; Ctrl-C
exits.

Qualified links can open HELP:USER.HLP or GAMES:GAMES.HLP while
parent/root navigation remembers their directories. The viewer supports
ordinary HLP and its supported compressed HZP files. // reports the
installed version/defaults.

CPMHELP and LBRHELP are different private historical help readers. This
page describes public HELPC.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
